# title: Compound option (call on a call)
# category: Choosers and compounds
# underlyings: 1
# source: Geske, The Valuation of Compound Options, Journal of Financial Economics, 1979
# source: Bouzoubaa & Osseiran, Exotic Options and Hybrids: A Guide to Structuring, Pricing and Trading, Wiley, 2010
# summary: The right, on the decision date, to buy a call by paying a premium: leverage on the call itself.
# param: strike = 1.0 | percent | Strike of the underlying call, % of the initial level
# param: premium = 0.05 | percent | Premium paid on the decision date for the call, % of the initial level
#
# The decision is an early-exercise right (a Longstaff-Schwartz regression on
# the spot): the price is a lower bound for the holder, priced on the CPU.

2027-01-04
    strike = 1.0
    premium = 0.05
    s0 = spot()
    held = 0

2027-07-06
    if exercise(spot()) then
        pays -premium * s0
        held = 1
    endIf

2028-01-04
    if held = 1 then pays max(spot() - strike * s0, 0) endIf
